### Topic 57 - RabbitMQ sample requests (VS Code "REST Client" extension)
### Start RabbitMQ first:  docker compose up -d
### Then watch the app log - the listeners print what they receive.
@base = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Place an order -> 202 Accepted; NotificationListener + AnalyticsListener log it
POST {{base}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Asha",
  "customerEmail": "asha@example.com",
  "product": "Laptop",
  "quantity": 1,
  "unitPrice": 899.99
}

### 2. An order whose email "fails" -> 3 attempts, then the message lands in the dead-letter queue
POST {{base}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Ravi",
  "customerEmail": "ravi@fail.test",
  "product": "Phone",
  "quantity": 2,
  "unitPrice": 250.00
}

### 3. Invalid order -> 400 Bad Request (validation, nothing is sent to RabbitMQ)
POST {{base}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "",
  "customerEmail": "not-an-email",
  "product": "Laptop",
  "quantity": 0,
  "unitPrice": 10
}

### 4. Cancel an order -> only the analytics queue receives it ("order.#" binding)
POST {{base}}/api/orders/abc-123/cancel?reason=found%20cheaper

### 5. Broadcast an announcement through the fanout exchange
POST {{base}}/api/announcements
Content-Type: text/plain

Big Diwali sale starts tomorrow!
